think Round-opened; no live claim named a path I intended to touch besides pheromone's own descriptor_test.rye claim, which I left alone.
think Launched the cold endurance run per the ORDER clause and found a stale in-flight pass from a prior lap whose launch_head was no longer HEAD; used the bounded fleet_call.sh (never a bare pkill) to TERM it, waited for the lock to clear, then relaunched fresh and held still -- no commit, no edit, no pull -- until run_verdict=.
think Read all 30 reds the cold run named. Most were already OPEN under other lanes' names or explicitly Keaton's word (the receipt-contract ceilings, the moonshot rank/falsifier meters, the index_row_bound backlog already booked as an unowned OPEN row). Two stood out as cheap and safe: rye/bin/rye and rishi/bin/rishi were stale against their own sources -- gitignored binaries, rebuilding them touches no tracked byte and carries no risk to peers.
think Read commit_parent_claim's evidence closely: the %801 wall, closed GREEN on 20260917.174536, already reads 29 violations of its own class since its anchor, because the witness runs only in the cold pass and tools/hooks/commit-msg carries no equivalent check at write time. This is squarely law-lane -- booked as REDS %826, OPEN, naming the fifth-wall question as the open door.
think Shelved my prior live INCENSE account (comment_path) to archive per the-writer-sheds before writing a new one, keeping one live account on the card.
think Committed, then round-opened again before push and hit a true divergence -- the local commit was parked on pier/diverged-20260918-075904 by the safety convention rather than lost. Cherry-picked it back onto the anointed HEAD, resolved one conflict in REDS.md (a peer had closed %825 while my commit still carried the stale OPEN text), re-ran reds_ledger_monotone/reds_row_present/itinerary_account_shelf/pin_bound_touch all GREEN, amended the Git nib per rule 2, and pushed both remotes.
obs The %801 finding is the more durable lesson: a wall proven GREEN at seating is a wall against everything written before it, not a standing gate, if nothing runs it at the moment the violation is written. Recorded rather than patched, since a hook change is shared across all eight ships and wants the owning lane's word.
obs tree_moved=no on the cold run itself, holding the ORDER clause's promise -- the only mover this lap met was the round-open pull between commit and push, which the diverged-branch safety net absorbed rather than losing anything.
